  "title": [
    "[The Graveyard Temporalis]"
  ],
  "description": [
    "Several large monuments stand in neat rows off the side of the path amid the thick overgrowth of grass and moss.  Candles have been arranged on the lower lip of some of the larger grave markers, and it is evident by the amount of wax coldly clinging to the stone as it meets the ground that these luminaries are regularly replaced.  They flicker fitfully from time to time, doing little to banish the foggy groundcover, instead only brightening it from within in fits and starts."
  ],
